, "move": "pass", "lead_before": -3.95, "lead_after": -3.96, "points_lost": 0.0, "best": "pass"}, {"turn": 94, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -3.96, "lead_after": -4.0, "points_lost": -0.04, "best": "pass"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A Seesaw Around the Right Edge", "summary": "The 12k won as White by 4 points after a game of enormous swings. Opus 5.5 fell behind through a run of 3-to-7-point losses in the opening and middle, then lost 18.5 on move 19 and was far behind. Both sides traded 30-point errors around the right edge (moves 48 to 56), and Black pulled back to -4.1 by move 57. The endgame was quiet, and the lead stayed near -4.0 until the two passes.", "moments": [{"turn": 19, "text": "Opus 5.5's G6 dropped the lead from -19.0 to -37.4, an 18.5-point loss. The engine preferred D6. Black was already well behind, and this turned a deficit into a deep hole."}, {"turn": 41, "text": "Opus 5.5 played J4 and lost 27.5 points, taking the lead from -25.8 to -53.3, the lowest of the game. The engine wanted B4. Two moves later J6 won back 23.2 points (-58.1 to -34.9), so the right-edge fight was far from over."}, {"turn": 48, "text": "The 12k's H8 was the largest error of the game, losing 36.7 points. It took the lead from -40.3 to -3.6, so a Black loss on the board became a game within a few points. The engine's choice was B5."}, {"turn": 49, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with H7, which lost 34.6 points (-3.6 to -38.2) and handed the swing straight back. The engine preferred B7. Opus 5.5 lost another 31.4 on move 51 and 30.4 on move 55, and the 12k recovered similar amounts on moves 50, 52 and 56."}, {"turn": 58, "text": "The 12k's J7 lost 4.3 points and put the lead at +0.1, the only moment Black was ahead. Opus 5.5's next move, D8, lost 2.3 and the lead went back to -2.2. By the end it sat near -4.0, matching the W+4 result."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties with a DANGER flag, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally area plus komi (optionally with named dead stones removed). Both only inspect the position the player supplied; neither generates, scores or ranks candidate moves, or plays any continuation.", "stop": false}}